From acac55ed1e17b6d29eef12133e0eaa0ba29b23de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Branch <andrewbranch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:41:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Reuse scanners across astnav child and token
 materialization

createChildren allocated a fresh scanner for every node whose children were
materialized, and the token lookups (getTokenAtPosition, findNextToken,
findPrecedingToken) allocated one per query. Keep a per-source-file pool of
idle scanners (WeakMap<SourceFile, Scanner[]>): check out by popping or
creating, reset text/language variant on checkout, and in a finally block
clear comment directives and token state before returning the scanner.
Scanners are removed from the pool while in use, so nested or reentrant
traversals always get distinct scanners.

Add tests covering reuse across cached/repeated calls and token lookups,
nested child creation, exceptions during child creation, trivia/comment
directives/JSDoc state, exact token boundaries, and independent source files
with different language variants.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
